Verse 1:
[D]An [Em]upper room [Bm]did [Am/C]our [D]Lord [Em]prepare
[G]For those [Bm]loved [Em]until [Am]the end:
[Em]And [D]His [C]disciples [D7/F#]still [G]gather [Em]there,
[D]To [Em]celebrate their [D]risen Friend.

Verse 2:
[D]And [Em]after supper [Am/C]He [D]washed [Em]their [Am/C]feet,
[G]For service, [Em]too, [C]is [Am]sacrament.
[Em]In [D]Him [C]our joy [Bm]shall [D7/F#]be [G]made [Em]complete
[D]Sent [Em]out [Am]to [Bm]serve, [Em]as [D]He was sent.

Verse 3:
[D]A [Em]lasting gift [Bm]Jesus [D]gave [Em]His [Am/C]own:
[G]To share [Bm]His [Em]bread, [C]His [Am]loving cup.
[Em]Whatever [C]burdens [D7/F#]may [G]bow [Em]us down,
[D]He [Em]by [Am]His [Bm]cross [Em]shall [D]lift us up.

Verse 4:
[D]No [Em]end there is! [Bm]we [Am/C]depart [Em]in [Am/C]peace.
[G]He loves [Em]beyond [C]our [Am]uttermost:
[Em]In [D]every [Bm]room [C/E]in [D7/F#]our [G]Father's [Em]house,
[D]He [Em]will [Am]be [Bm]there, [Em]as [D]Lord and host.
